The 4yr cycle is 3 years of a bull market and 1 year of a bear.

The last quarter of the bear, is part of the bear. That's literally the part where you're supposed to buy back in.

Missing the point of maximum opportunity by a full quarter is a shockingly bad accuracy. If you had of sold the 'top' a quarter early in 2017 you would have sold at $4k...the floor of the bear. If you sold a quarter early in 2021 you'd have sold at $29k, barely high enough to justify the taxes selling to buy in the bear.

A full quarter is a massive delta, and it's just plain wrong.

Folks are literally poorer because they missed the signs due to this nonsense idea that the calendar drives the price.

@TA_On_Chain Spend 10mins with your local LLM.

Ask it how much of the cycle return you miss by missing the low by a full quarter.

Also ask it how much of the bull return you miss by selling a quarter early, and then a quarter late.

A full quarter off on a system like this, is dead wrong.

